From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Thomson <git@mnt.dev>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 19:42:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [garmin] Turn-by-turn navigation on watch

Adds om-nav, a Connect IQ watch app showing the next turn arrow, the distance
to that turn, the street being turned onto, distance and arrival time for the
whole route, and a buzz as each turn comes up; plus the phone-side bridge that
feeds it.

NavigationService gains a NavigationConsumer interface so live navigation
state can be mirrored outside the app without the service knowing about
wearables. The new :libs:garmin module implements it over the Connect IQ
Mobile SDK, which reaches the watch through the Garmin Connect app over
Bluetooth -- no Garmin servers and no Google Play services are involved.

The watch's turn constants and the CarDirection ordinals on the phone have to
agree or messages are drawn wrong; GarminNavStateTest pins them so a mismatch
fails the Android build.

See garmin/README.md for the Connect IQ toolchain, building and sideloading --
the watch app is not part of the Gradle build.
